   "stem": {
      "text": "Let f(x) = x e^(sin(3x)). What is the value of f'(pi/3)?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": [
         "Subtract",
         1,
         "Pi"
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "f is a product of x and the composite e^(sin(3x)), so f'(x) = e^(sin(3x)) + x d/dx[e^(sin(3x))].",
         "mathjson": [
            "Exp",
            [
               "Sin",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  3,
                  "x"
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The composite has three layers: the exponential gives e^(sin(3x)), the sine gives cos(3x), and 3x gives 3. So f'(x) = e^(sin(3x)) (1 + 3x cos(3x)).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Exp",
               [
                  "Sin",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     3,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               1,
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  3,
                  "x",
                  [
                     "Cos",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        3,
                        "x"
                     ]
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = pi/3 the innermost value is 3x = pi, where sin(pi) = 0 and cos(pi) = -1, so e^(sin(3x)) = 1.",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Substitute: f'(pi/3) = 1 (1 + 3(pi/3)(-1)) = 1 - pi.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Subtract",
            1,
            "Pi"
         ]
      }
   ],
